# Merge strategies for the parallel-session conflict magnets
# (see meta/issues/generated-artifact-merge-conflicts.md).
#
# Append-only listings: the common conflict is two sessions inserting entries
# at the same anchor; git's built-in union driver keeps both sides' lines.
# (Generic rule first — later, more specific lines override it.)
index.md merge=union

# Generated artifacts: never 3-way-merge their text — the right resolution is
# "re-derive from the merged sources". The `regen` driver resolves as `ours`
# at merge time (configured by .claude/hooks/session-start.sh:
# `git config merge.regen.driver true`); `mix brain.regen` then re-derives
# every generated artifact, and the pre-commit/CI freshness gates reject the
# merge commit until that has happened. Without the driver configured, git
# falls back to the default text merge — at worst today's behavior.
CLAUDE.md merge=regen
meta/registry.md merge=regen
meta/code-map.md merge=regen
meta/flows/lineage.md merge=regen
beliefs/glossary/index.md merge=regen
